## CSS (UI Styling) Guidelines

### Property Order Convention

Follow the structured order below to maintain consistency and readability across all CSS files:

-   **Display & Layout**: Properties like: `display`, `position`, `top/right/bottom/left`, `flex`, `grid`, `z-index`, `overflow`, `visibility`.
-   **Box Model & Backgrounds**: Properties like: `width`, `height`, `margin`, `padding`, `box-sizing`, `border`, `border-radius`, `outline`, `background-color`, `background-image`, `background-*`.
-   **Typography**: Properties like: `font-family`, `font-weight`, `font-size`, `font-style`, `color`, `line-height`, `letter-spacing`, `text-align`, `text-decoration`, `text-transform`, `white-space`.
-   **Visual Effects**: Properties like: `cursor`, `opacity`, `box-shadow`, `transform`, `filter`, `pointer-events`.
-   **Transitions & Animations**
-   **Pseudo-elements & pseudo-classes**: Properties like: `::before`, `::after`, `:hover`, `:focus`, `:active`
-   **Media queries**

💡 Tips: Use spacing and line breaks wisely to separate logical groups, especially in large style blocks. This enhances clarity and makes overrides easier to spot during debugging.
